Help For The Wi-Fi Setup

Wi-Fi setup: s w from the main menu. Nothing is applied until y confirms connection at Connect Y/N?. n returns to edit the details; q cancels.

Aborted: entry was cancelled or the network name was empty. Entered details are discarded; return to Settings. Repeat w there, or s w from the main menu, to try again.
Connected: Wi-Fi connected and saved; this does not confirm internet access.
Connecting: connection is in progress; it may take two minutes.
Country: enter the two-letter code. UK is accepted as GB. Blank Enter keeps the current country, if available.
Ctrl+C: cancel from any field. At confirmation, q also cancels.
e: at confirmation, return to the fields for editing.
h: at Country, type h then Enter for help; at confirmation, press h. Help returns to the same prompt.
Invalid: an entry could not be accepted. The request ends and entered details are discarded. Return to Settings; repeat w to try again with valid details.
Network name: enter the exact SSID, 1 to 32 UTF-8 bytes, without control characters. Blank Enter aborts.
Password: entry is hidden; Speakup key echo is temporarily off and restored afterwards. Blank means an open network, not cancellation. Letters such as h and q, spaces and punctuation are literal in network names and passwords.
y: at Connect Y/N?, connect and save. n returns to edit; q cancels. Until then, cancelling or invalid entry leaves the connection unchanged.

